# rejoinFunction(String username)
#
# Cleans up after a player who logged off mid-cutscene: their pig went offline
# with them and comes back with them on rejoin.
#
# HOW THIS IS TRIGGERED (three designs were tried; only this one works):
#  1. WorldGuard console-command-on-entry + "%username%"  -- REJECTED. This
#     server does not substitute %username%; the script received the literal
#     string, Player("%username%") gave a null UUID, and the first method call
#     threw "IllegalArgumentException: UUID id cannot be null".
#  2. WorldGuard console-command-on-entry + Region.getPlayersInside() -- also
#     REJECTED. Entry flags fire on BOUNDARY CROSSING, a movement event. A
#     relogging player is already inside the region, crosses nothing, and the
#     flag never fires. Confirmed empirically: walking out and back in works,
#     relogging does not.
#  3. /login action add  -- WHAT WE USE. startAnimation queues this at the
#     moment it detects the logout, while it still holds the Player object, so
#     the username is baked in as a LITERAL here. No placeholder substitution
#     is involved anywhere, and login actions fire on login by definition.
#
# OTHER INVARIANTS:
#  - Player(username) resolves name -> UUID AT CONSTRUCTION. On login that
#    lookup is too early, so the @delay MUST come BEFORE the Player(...) line.
#    Delaying after it just uses an already-null UUID -- that was the original
#    bug and the reason "adding a delay" appeared not to help.
#  - Runs from console: no @bypass executor, so every command is @console with
#    explicit selectors. Relative forms (~ ~ ~, @s, distance=..) have nothing
#    to anchor to here.
#  - Vanilla /tp takes no world argument; dimension comes from /execute in.

@using lavamap
@fast

# Let the join settle before touching the player registry.
@delay 10

@define Player p = Player(username)
@if p.isOnline() == false
    @return
@fi

# Idempotence guard. A queued login action may outlive the situation that
# created it -- without this, a stale action could yank a player who has since
# started a fresh cutscene.
@if loggedOffMidCutscene[p] != 1
    @return
@fi

# Kill the pig they are actually riding. "on vehicle" (1.19.4+) resolves the
# mount directly, so this needs no tag bookkeeping and no-ops harmlessly if
# they came back un-mounted.
@console /execute as {{username}} on vehicle run kill @s

# Fallback for pre-1.19.4 servers -- tag-based, needs lastPigNumber to have
# survived the logout:
# @console /execute in minecraft:theta run kill @e[tag=lavamappig{{lastPigNumber[p]}}]

@console /execute in minecraft:theta run tp {{username}} -13088.237548828125 94.0 9478.935546875 90.0 -1.3685483

@var loggedOffMidCutscene[p] = 0
